because $\\frac{z-4}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, in our line, the $z$ component always maintains the constant value of $z=4.$ For example, our two points $P(7,-2,4)$ and $Q(1,1,4)$ both have $z$-coordinates of $z=4.$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{z-4}{0}$ part and instead write $z=4,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{-6}=\\frac{y+2}{3},\\,z=4\n$$" 13194139534873 true] [17592186316475 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316476 13194139534873 true] [17592186316475 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316477 13194139534873 true] [17592186316475 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316478 13194139534873 true] [17592186316475 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316479 13194139534873 true] [17592186316475 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316480 13194139534873 true] [17592186316475 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534873 true] [17592186316475 1041 "selection" 13194139534873 true] [17592186316475 1104 #edb/ref 17592186316478 13194139534873 true] [17592186316475 1110 #uuid "a25ad256-2afe-542f-bd14-1da74a18de5e" 13194139534873 true] [17592186316476 1034 "\\frac{x-7}{6}=\\frac{y-2}{3},\\,z=4" 13194139534873 true] [17592186316476 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534873 true] [17592186316476 1111 #uuid "035a6874-6c4b-5495-a0cd-db32991e6815" 13194139534873 true] [17592186316477 1034 "\\frac{x+7}{-6}=\\frac{y-2}{-3},\\,z=-4" 13194139534873 true] [17592186316477 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534873 true] [17592186316477 1111 #uuid "a290a146-754d-5108-a099-f99363cd7ac6" 13194139534873 true] [17592186316478 1034 "\\frac{x-7}{-6}=\\frac{y+2}{3},\\,z=4" 13194139534873 true] [17592186316478 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534873 true] [17592186316478 1111 #uuid "000edebc-1e5e-52b0-a9de-f20fe0034291" 13194139534873 true] [17592186316479 1034 "\\frac{x+7}{-6}=\\frac{y+2}{-3},\\,z=4" 13194139534873 true] [17592186316479 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534873 true] [17592186316479 1111 #uuid "40116425-bfed-5f5a-ab95-3e4695a81e95" 13194139534873 true] [17592186316480 1034 "\\frac{x-7}{6}=\\frac{y